module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.ProjInvertibleTwist
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistBaseChange.Iso

/-!
# Clause (1) of Tag 02NC without a global generator of the twisting module

Let `R` be a commutative ring, `𝒜` a graded `R`-algebra, `𝓛` a family of tensor powers of an
**invertible** `R`-module `ℒ = 𝓛 1` inside a commutative ring `T`, and `ℬ` the twist of `𝒜` by
`𝓛`, so that `ℬ d` is `𝒜 d ⊗_R 𝓛 d`. Clause (1) of
[Stacks, Tag 02NC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NC) asserts that the comparison maps
`θ_n` on the `n`-th twisting sheaves are isomorphisms.

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Constructions/ProjInvertibleTwist.lean` proves that clause under
the extra hypothesis that `ℒ` has a **global generator** `ℓ`, as
`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.isIso_twistMap`. **This file removes that hypothesis.** For
*every* degree-one element `ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1`, with no generation assumption, the comparison map
`θ_n` attached to `ψ_ℓ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ`, `x ↦ x ⊗ ℓ ^ d`, is an isomorphism over the domain of
definition `U(ψ_ℓ) ⊆ Proj ℬ`, and those domains cover `Proj ℬ`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.isIso_twistMap_twistHomOf`: **clause (1) of Tag 02NC in the
  absolute case with no global generator**, for every `ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1` and every `n : ℤ`.
* `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.iSup_mapDomain_twistHomOf_eq_top`: **its scope**, the opens
  `U(ψ_ℓ)` cover `Proj ℬ` as `ℓ` ranges over `𝓛 1`. This is what replaces
  `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.mapDomain_twistHom_eq_top`, which says that a *single* `ℓ`
  suffices when it generates.
* `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.exists_dual_notMem`: **the reason the generation hypothesis
  is removable** — at every point of `U(ψ_ℓ)` some functional `μ` on `𝓛 1` has `μ ℓ` omitted by
  the point, so `ℓ` trivializes `𝓛 1` there.
* `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.injective_twistFibreMap` and
  `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.fractionLift`: the two pointwise inputs of
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistBaseChange.isIso_twistMap_of_inputs`.
* `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.isOpenImmersion_mapHom_twistHomOf`: its third input.
* `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.exists_smul_pow_eq_twistHomOf` and
  `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.exists_smul_pow_eq_zero`: the comparison attached to `ℓ` is
  surjective, respectively injective, after multiplication by a power of `μ ℓ` — not degreewise,
  as in the companion file, but on all of `B` and all of `A`.
* `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.exists_notMem_mul_eq_zero`: the kernel transfer, the one
  step that is not formal.

## The route

Invertibility of `θ_n` is **not** proved from a degreewise bijectivity of `ψ_ℓ`, which is false
without a generator: `x ↦ x ⊗ ℓ ^ d` is bijective exactly when `ℓ` generates. The route is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistBaseChange.isIso_twistMap_of_inputs`, whose three inputs are
pointwise or local and are therefore insensitive to the absence of a *global* trivialization.

* The induced morphism `U(ψ_ℓ) ⟶ Proj 𝒜` is an **open immersion** because it is the restriction
  of the canonical isomorphism
  `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.projTwistGlued` — that is
  `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.ι_comp_projTwistGlued`. Nothing has to be
  proved about the morphism itself.
* The **fibre comparison is injective** at every point of `U(ψ_ℓ)`. The fibre comparison is the
  map `A_𝔭 → B_𝔮` of localizations at a homogeneous prime of `B` and its `ψ_ℓ`-contraction, so
  injectivity is the statement that an element of `A` whose image is killed by something the
  point omits is itself killed by something whose image the point omits. That is
  `exists_notMem_mul_eq_zero`, and it uses both halves of the trivialization at the point: the
  annihilator is turned into an image of `ψ_ℓ` after multiplying by a power of `μ ℓ`
  (`exists_smul_pow_eq_twistHomOf`), and the resulting element of the kernel of `ψ_ℓ` is killed
  by a power of `μ ℓ` (`exists_smul_pow_eq_zero`).
* **Homogeneous fractions lift** pointwise: numerator and denominator each become images after
  multiplication by a power of `μ ℓ`, and the two exponents are exchanged, exactly as in
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistBaseChange.exists_fraction_lift` for a localization.

What makes all three available is `exists_dual_notMem`: a point of `U(ψ_ℓ)` omits `ψ_ℓ f`
for some homogeneous `f` of positive degree, and `ℓ ^ d` lies in the ideal generated by the
values `μ_i ℓ` of a trivializing family of `𝓛 1` — because `ℓ = ∑ μ_i(ℓ) • m_i` by the symmetry
`μ x • y = μ y • x` of `Stacks.GradedRing.IsTensorPowerFamily.smul_comm_of_dual` — so the point
must omit one of those values. In other words a generator of `𝓛 1` exists at every point where
clause (1) has anything to say, and the hypothesis `hgen` of the companion file was a global
version of a local fact.

The passage from the degreewise statements of the companion file
(`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.exists_mem_twistHomOf_eq_smul`,
`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.smul_pow_eq_zero_of_twistHomOf_eq_zero`) to statements about
arbitrary elements is the graded decomposition, with the exponent taken to be the supremum of
the support; the injective half uses that a graded ring homomorphism commutes with the
decomposition, `GradedRingHom.map_directSumDecompose`.

## What this does not reach

* **The relative case.** Everything here is absolute: `R` a ring, `Proj` the absolute
  homogeneous spectrum. See the "Scope, against the source" paragraph of
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Constructions/ProjInvertibleTwist.lean` for the relative
  obstruction.
* **A single `θ_n` for the glued isomorphism.** The source's clause (1) is one comparison
  `g^*𝒪_{P'}(n) ≅ 𝒪_P(n) ⊗ π^*ℒ^{⊗ n}` for the canonical isomorphism
  `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.projTwistIsoGeneral`. What is proved here is that
  comparison *read on the cover* `{U(ψ_ℓ)}`, where the factor `π^*ℒ^{⊗ n}` is trivialized by
  `ℓ ^ n` and so does not appear:
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistCompare.twistMap` has no room for it. The cocycle identity
  on `U(ψ_ℓ) ⊓ U(ψ_{ℓ'})`, whose algebraic input would be
  `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.twistHomOf_mul_comm`, is **not** the only thing missing.
  The object `π^*ℒ^{⊗ n}` is available, and morphisms of sheaves of modules do glue
  over an open cover
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleHomGlue.existsUnique_hom_of_restrict_cover`); what does not
  exist is the chartwise comparison that would be glued. `twistMap n` has target
  `(pullback ι_ℓ).obj (𝒪_P(n))` with no tensor factor, so turning it into a morphism to
  `(pullback ι_ℓ).obj (𝒪_P(n) ⊗ π^*ℒ^{⊗ n})` first needs the **trivialization of `π^*ℒ^{⊗ n}`
  over `U(ψ_ℓ)` by `ℓ ^ n`**, which the library does not have. The cocycle identity is an
  identity *between two such trivializations* and cannot be stated before they exist. See the
  corresponding paragraph of
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Constructions/ProjInvertibleTwist.lean` for the four steps that
  precede it; the algebraic core of the first is
  `Stacks.GradedRing.IsTensorPowerFamily.smul_pow_eq_dualPow_smul`.
* **Clause (2) read in the object `𝒪_P(n) ⊗ π^*ℒ^{⊗ n}`.** Clause (2) is proved for an
  arbitrary section of `ℒ^{⊗ n}` by
  `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.twistMap_degreeSection_piece` and its two corollaries, but
  always read through the trivialization by `ℓ ^ n`; nothing here changes that, and the
  obstruction to reading it in the object itself is the one above.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02NC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N3)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe u

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry DirectSum Graded HomogeneousIdeal
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistChain
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistCompare Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistBaseChange
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj
open scoped TensorProduct

namespace Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist

attribute [local instance] ProjectiveSpectrum.isPrime

/-- A product `ρ ^ M * (ρ ^ N * t)` of powers of `ρ` and `t` avoids a prime if `ρ` and `t` do. -/
private theorem pow_mul_pow_mul_notMem {B : Type u} [CommRing B] {P : Ideal B}
    (hP : P.IsPrime) {ρ t : B} (hρ : ρ ∉ P) (ht : t ∉ P) (M N : ℕ) : ρ ^ M * (ρ ^ N * t) ∉ P :=
  fun h => hP.mul_notMem (fun h' => hρ (hP.mem_of_pow_mem M h'))
    (hP.mul_notMem (fun h' => hρ (hP.mem_of_pow_mem N h')) ht) h

variable {R A B T : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing T]
  [Algebra R A] [Algebra R B] [Algebra R T]
  {𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A} [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] {𝓛 : ℕ → Submodule R T}
  {ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R B} [GradedAlgebra ℬ] (tw : InvertibleTwist 𝒜 𝓛 ℬ)
  (h𝓛 : IsTensorPowerFamily 𝓛) {ℓ : T}

include tw h𝓛

/-! ### A degree-one element is trivializing wherever its comparison is defined -/

/-- **A degree-one element is a sum of a trivializing family's elements with coefficients its
own values under their functionals.** For `∑ μ_i m_i = 1` and any `ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1` the symmetry
`μ x • y = μ y • x` gives `ℓ = ∑ μ_i(ℓ) • m_i`. -/
theorem sum_dual_smul_eq (hℓ : ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1)
    (s : Finset ((Module.Dual R (𝓛 1)) × (𝓛 1))) (hs : ∑ p ∈ s, p.1 p.2 = 1) :
    ∑ p ∈ s, (p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) • ((p.2 : T)) = ℓ := by
  have h1 : ∑ p ∈ s, (p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) • p.2 = (⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ : 𝓛 1) := by
    refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun p _ => h𝓛.smul_comm_of_dual p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ p.2) ?_
    rw [← Finset.sum_smul, hs, one_smul]
  have h2 := congrArg (fun x : 𝓛 1 => (x : T)) h1
  refine Eq.trans ?_ h2
  exact (map_sum (𝓛 1).subtype (fun p => (p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) • p.2) s).symm

/-- **Wherever the comparison attached to `ℓ` is defined, `ℓ` trivializes the twisting module.**
At a point of `U(ψ_ℓ) ⊆ Proj ℬ` some functional `μ` on `𝓛 1` has `μ ℓ` invertible, in the sense
that the point omits its image in `B`.

This is the precise sense in which no *global* generator of `𝓛 1` is needed for clause (1) of
Tag 02NC: a generator is available at every point where the clause has anything to say. The
argument is that `ℓ ^ d` lies in the ideal generated by the values `μ_i ℓ` of a trivializing
family, by `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.sum_dual_smul_eq`, so a point omitting
`ψ_ℓ f = f ⊗ ℓ ^ d` must omit one of those values. -/
theorem exists_dual_notMem [Module.Invertible R ↥(𝓛 1)] (hℓ : ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1)
    (q : ProjectiveSpectrum ℬ) (hq : q ∈ mapDomain 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ)) :
    ∃ μ : (𝓛 1) →ₗ[R] R, algebraMap R B (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ∉ q.asHomogeneousIdeal := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_finset_dual_sum_eq_one (R := R) (𝓛 1)
  obtain ⟨d, f, hd, hf, hfq⟩ := (mem_mapDomain_iff 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) q).mp hq
  by_contra hcon
  have hcon' : ∀ μ : (𝓛 1) →ₗ[R] R,
      algebraMap R B (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ∈ q.asHomogeneousIdeal := fun μ => by
    by_contra h
    exact hcon ⟨μ, h⟩
  obtain ⟨e, rfl⟩ : ∃ e, d = e + 1 := ⟨d - 1, by omega⟩
  have hMmem : ∀ p : (Module.Dual R (𝓛 1)) × (𝓛 1), ℓ ^ e * (p.2 : T) ∈ 𝓛 (e + 1) := fun p => by
    rw [← h𝓛.mul_eq e 1]
    exact Submodule.mul_mem_mul (h𝓛.pow_mem hℓ e) p.2.2
  have hL : (⟨ℓ ^ (e + 1), h𝓛.pow_mem hℓ (e + 1)⟩ : 𝓛 (e + 1)) =
      ∑ p ∈ s, (p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) • (⟨ℓ ^ e * (p.2 : T), hMmem p⟩ : 𝓛 (e + 1)) := by
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (map_sum (𝓛 (e + 1)).subtype
      (fun p => (p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) • (⟨ℓ ^ e * (p.2 : T), hMmem p⟩ : 𝓛 (e + 1))) s).symm
    simp only [Submodule.subtype_apply]
    have hterm : ∀ p : (Module.Dual R (𝓛 1)) × (𝓛 1),
        ((((p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) • (⟨ℓ ^ e * (p.2 : T), hMmem p⟩ : 𝓛 (e + 1))) : 𝓛 (e + 1)) : T) =
          ℓ ^ e * ((p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) • (p.2 : T)) := by
      intro p
      rw [Submodule.coe_smul]
      show (p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) • (ℓ ^ e * (p.2 : T)) = _
      rw [Algebra.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def]
      ring
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun p _ => hterm p, ← Finset.mul_sum,
      tw.sum_dual_smul_eq h𝓛 hℓ s hs, pow_succ]
  refine hfq ?_
  rw [tw.twistHomOf_apply_of_mem h𝓛 hℓ hf, hL]
  have hexp : (tw.piece (e + 1) (⟨f, hf⟩ ⊗ₜ[R]
        ∑ p ∈ s, (p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) • (⟨ℓ ^ e * (p.2 : T), hMmem p⟩ : 𝓛 (e + 1))) : B) =
      ∑ p ∈ s, algebraMap R B (p.1 ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) *
        (tw.piece (e + 1) (⟨f, hf⟩ ⊗ₜ[R] (⟨ℓ ^ e * (p.2 : T), hMmem p⟩ : 𝓛 (e + 1))) : B) := by
    rw [TensorProduct.tmul_sum]
    rw [map_sum]
    refine Eq.trans (map_sum (ℬ (e + 1)).subtype _ s) ?_
    simp only [Submodule.subtype_apply]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun p _ => ?_
    rw [TensorProduct.tmul_smul, map_smul, Submodule.coe_smul, Algebra.smul_def]
  rw [hexp]
  refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun p _ => Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ ?_
  exact hcon' p.1

/-! ### The comparison attached to `ℓ` is a localization away from `μ ℓ` -/

/-- **Every element of `B` becomes an image of the comparison after multiplication by a power of
`μ ℓ`.** The element is a finite sum of homogeneous pieces, each of which becomes an image after
multiplying by the power of `μ ℓ` named by its own degree. -/
theorem exists_smul_pow_eq_twistHomOf (μ : (𝓛 1) →ₗ[R] R) (hℓ : ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1) (b : B) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (x : A), (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ^ N • b = tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ x := by
  classical
  have key : ∀ d : ℕ, ∃ x : A, x ∈ 𝒜 d ∧
      (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ^ d • ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ b d : ℬ d) : B) = tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ x :=
    fun d => tw.exists_mem_twistHomOf_eq_smul h𝓛 μ hℓ d (DirectSum.decompose ℬ b d).2
  choose x hx hxe using key
  set S := (DirectSum.decompose ℬ b).support with hS
  refine ⟨S.sup id, ∑ d ∈ S, (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ^ (S.sup id - d) • x d, ?_⟩
  rw [map_sum]
  conv_lhs => rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_decompose ℬ b]
  rw [Finset.smul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun d hd => ?_
  have hdle : d ≤ S.sup id := Finset.le_sup (f := id) hd
  rw [tw.twistHomOf_smul_of_mem h𝓛 hℓ _ (hx d), ← hxe d, smul_smul, ← pow_add,
    Nat.sub_add_cancel hdle]

/-- **The comparison attached to `ℓ` is injective after multiplication by a power of `μ ℓ`.**
A graded ring homomorphism commutes with the graded decomposition, so an element killed by the
comparison has every homogeneous piece killed by it, and
`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.smul_pow_eq_zero_of_twistHomOf_eq_zero` applies to each. -/
theorem exists_smul_pow_eq_zero (μ : (𝓛 1) →ₗ[R] R) (hℓ : ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1) {a : A}
    (ha : tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ a = 0) : ∃ N : ℕ, (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ^ N • a = 0 := by
  classical
  set S := (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 a).support with hS
  refine ⟨S.sup id, ?_⟩
  conv_lhs => rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_decompose 𝒜 a]
  rw [Finset.smul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun d hd => ?_
  have hdle : d ≤ S.sup id := Finset.le_sup (f := id) hd
  have hzero : tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ ((DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 a d : 𝒜 d) : A) = 0 := by
    rw [GradedRingHom.map_directSumDecompose, ha]
    simp
  have hd0 := tw.smul_pow_eq_zero_of_twistHomOf_eq_zero h𝓛 μ hℓ
    (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 a d).2 hzero
  rw [show S.sup id = (S.sup id - d) + d by omega, pow_add, ← smul_smul, hd0, smul_zero]

/-! ### The fibre comparison is injective -/

/-- **The kernel transfer.** At a point of `U(ψ_ℓ)`, an element of `A` whose image is killed by
something the point omits is itself killed by something whose image the point omits.

This is the one genuinely non-formal step. Both halves of the trivialization are used: the
annihilator `t` is first turned into an image `ψ τ` after multiplying by a power of `μ ℓ`, and
then the resulting element `τ * a` of the kernel of `ψ` is killed by a power of `μ ℓ`. -/
theorem exists_notMem_mul_eq_zero [Module.Invertible R ↥(𝓛 1)] (hℓ : ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1)
    (q : ProjectiveSpectrum ℬ) (hq : q ∈ mapDomain 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ))
    {a : A} {t : B} (ht : t ∉ q.asHomogeneousIdeal)
    (hta : t * tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ a = 0) :
    ∃ u : A, tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ u ∉ q.asHomogeneousIdeal ∧ u * a = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨μ, hμ⟩ := tw.exists_dual_notMem h𝓛 hℓ q hq
  obtain ⟨N, τ, hτ⟩ := tw.exists_smul_pow_eq_twistHomOf h𝓛 μ hℓ t
  have hψτ : tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ τ = algebraMap R B (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ^ N * t := by
    rw [← hτ, Algebra.smul_def, map_pow]
  have hψτa : tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ (τ * a) = 0 := by
    rw [map_mul, hψτ, mul_assoc, hta, mul_zero]
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := tw.exists_smul_pow_eq_zero h𝓛 μ hℓ hψτa
  refine ⟨algebraMap R A (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ M) * τ, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hval : tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ (algebraMap R A (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ M) * τ) =
        algebraMap R B (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ^ M * (algebraMap R B (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ^ N * t) := by
      rw [map_mul, tw.twistHomOf_algebraMap h𝓛 hℓ, hψτ, map_pow]
    rw [hval]
    exact pow_mul_pow_mul_notMem q.isPrime hμ ht M N
  · have hval : algebraMap R A (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ M) * τ * a = (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ^ M • (τ * a) := by
      rw [Algebra.smul_def, map_pow, mul_assoc]
    rw [hval, hM]

/-- **The comparison on the fibres of the twisting sheaves is injective at every point of
`U(ψ_ℓ)`**, with no generation hypothesis on `ℓ`. The fibre comparison is the map
`A_𝔭 → B_𝔮` of localizations at a homogeneous prime and its `ψ_ℓ`-contraction, and injectivity
is the kernel transfer. -/
theorem injective_twistFibreMap [Module.Invertible R ↥(𝓛 1)] (hℓ : ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1)
    (y : (mapDomain 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ)).toScheme) :
    Function.Injective (twistFibreMap 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y) := by
  have hcomap : ∀ c : A,
      c ∉ (basePoint 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y).asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal ↔
        tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ c ∉
          (ambientPoint 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y).asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal := by
    have h : (basePoint 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y).asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal =
        Ideal.comap (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ : A →+* B)
          (ambientPoint 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y).asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal :=
      mapHom_base_toIdeal 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y
    intro c
    rw [h]
    exact not_congr Ideal.mem_comap
  intro X Y
  induction X, Y using LocalizedModule.induction_on₂ with
  | h a a' sa sa' =>
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := sa
    obtain ⟨s', hs'⟩ := sa'
    intro hXY
    have hψs : tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ s ∉
        (ambientPoint 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y).asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal :=
      (hcomap s).mp hs
    have hψs' : tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ s' ∉
        (ambientPoint 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y).asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal :=
      (hcomap s').mp hs'
    rw [twistFibreMap_mk 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y a s hs hψs,
      twistFibreMap_mk 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y a' s' hs' hψs',
      LocalizedModule.mk_eq] at hXY
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hXY
    simp only [Submonoid.smul_def, smul_eq_mul] at hu
    have hta : (u : B) * tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ (s' * a - s * a') = 0 := by
      rw [map_sub, map_mul, map_mul, mul_sub, hu, sub_self]
    obtain ⟨v, hv1, hv2⟩ := tw.exists_notMem_mul_eq_zero h𝓛 hℓ
      (ambientPoint 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y) y.2 u.2 hta
    refine LocalizedModule.mk_eq.mpr ⟨⟨v, (hcomap v).mpr hv1⟩, ?_⟩
    simp only [Submonoid.smul_def, smul_eq_mul]
    linear_combination hv2

/-! ### Homogeneous fractions lift pointwise -/

/-- **Homogeneous fractions lift pointwise along the comparison attached to `ℓ`**, with no
generation hypothesis. Both the numerator and the denominator of the target fraction become
images after multiplication by a power of `μ ℓ`, and the two exponents are then exchanged, so
that the numerator keeps its twisted degree and the denominator its degree. -/
theorem fractionLift [Module.Invertible R ↥(𝓛 1)] (hℓ : ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1) :
    FractionLift 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) := by
  intro y m K b s hb hs hsy
  obtain ⟨μ, hμ⟩ := tw.exists_dual_notMem h𝓛 hℓ (ambientPoint 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y) y.2
  obtain ⟨γ, hγ, hγe⟩ := tw.exists_mem_twistHomOf_eq_smul h𝓛 μ hℓ K hs
  have halg : ∀ k : ℕ, algebraMap R A (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ k) ∈ 𝒜 0 := fun k => by
    have h : algebraMap R A (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ k) = (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ k) • (1 : A) := by
      rw [Algebra.smul_def, mul_one]
    rw [h]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (SetLike.one_mem_graded 𝒜)
  have hmul : ∀ k : ℕ, algebraMap R A (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ k) * γ ∈ 𝒜 K := fun k => by
    have h := SetLike.mul_mem_graded (halg k) hγ
    rwa [zero_add] at h
  have hnot : ∀ k : ℕ, tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ (algebraMap R A (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ k) * γ) ∉
      (ambientPoint 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y).asHomogeneousIdeal := by
    intro k
    have hval : tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ (algebraMap R A (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ k) * γ) =
        algebraMap R B (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ^ k * (algebraMap R B (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩) ^ K * s) := by
      rw [map_mul, tw.twistHomOf_algebraMap h𝓛 hℓ, ← hγe, Algebra.smul_def, map_pow, map_pow]
    rw [hval]
    exact pow_mul_pow_mul_notMem (ambientPoint 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ) y).isPrime hμ hsy k K
  by_cases hi : 0 ≤ (K : ℤ) + m
  · have hb' : b ∈ ℬ ((K : ℤ) + m).toNat := by
      simpa [integerGrading, hi] using hb
    obtain ⟨β₀, hβ₀, hβ₀e⟩ := tw.exists_mem_twistHomOf_eq_smul h𝓛 μ hℓ
      ((K : ℤ) + m).toNat hb'
    refine ⟨(μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ K) • β₀, algebraMap R A (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ ((K : ℤ) + m).toNat) * γ, ?_,
      hmul _, hnot _, ?_⟩
    · have h : (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ K) • β₀ ∈ 𝒜 ((K : ℤ) + m).toNat := Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hβ₀
      simpa [integerGrading, hi] using h
    · rw [tw.twistHomOf_smul_of_mem h𝓛 hℓ _ hβ₀, ← hβ₀e, map_mul,
        tw.twistHomOf_algebraMap h𝓛 hℓ, ← hγe]
      simp only [Algebra.smul_def, map_pow]
      ring
  · have hb0 : b = 0 := by
      have h : b ∈ (⊥ : Submodule ℤ B) := by simpa [integerGrading, hi] using hb
      simpa using h
    refine ⟨0, algebraMap R A (μ ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩ ^ 0) * γ, zero_mem _, hmul _, hnot _, ?_⟩
    rw [hb0, map_zero, mul_zero, mul_zero]

/-! ### Clause (1) of Tag 02NC without a global generator -/

/-- **The morphism of homogeneous spectra attached to an arbitrary degree-one element is an open
immersion.** It is the restriction of the canonical isomorphism
`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.projTwistGlued` to the open `U(ψ_ℓ)`, by
`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.ι_comp_projTwistGlued`. -/
theorem isOpenImmersion_mapHom_twistHomOf [Module.Invertible R ↥(𝓛 1)] (hℓ : ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1) :
    IsOpenImmersion (mapHom 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ)) := by
  have : IsIso (tw.projTwistGlued h𝓛) := tw.isIso_projTwistGlued h𝓛
  rw [← tw.ι_comp_projTwistGlued h𝓛 hℓ]
  infer_instance

/-- **Clause (1) of Stacks Tag 02NC in the absolute case, with no global generator of the
twisting module.** For *every* degree-one element `ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1` the comparison map `θ n` on the
`n`-th twisting sheaf attached to `ψ_ℓ` is an isomorphism, for every `n : ℤ`, over the domain of
definition `U(ψ_ℓ) ⊆ Proj ℬ`.

`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.isIso_twistMap` is the same statement under the hypothesis
that `ℓ` generates `𝓛 1`, where `U(ψ_ℓ)` is the whole of `Proj ℬ`. The generation hypothesis is
discharged here, not weakened: it was used only to make `ψ_ℓ` bijective in each degree, and what
the comparison on twists really needs is the three *pointwise* inputs of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistBaseChange.isIso_twistMap_of_inputs`, each of which is available
at every point of `U(ψ_ℓ)` because `ℓ` trivializes `𝓛 1` there
(`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.exists_dual_notMem`).

The domains `U(ψ_ℓ)` cover `Proj ℬ` as `ℓ` ranges over `𝓛 1`
(`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.iSup_mapDomain_twistHomOf_eq_top`), so this is a statement
about the whole of `Proj ℬ` read on a cover, not about one open part of it. -/
theorem isIso_twistMap_twistHomOf [Module.Invertible R ↥(𝓛 1)] (hℓ : ℓ ∈ 𝓛 1) (n : ℤ) :
    IsIso ((projMapData 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ)).twistMap n) := by
  have := tw.isOpenImmersion_mapHom_twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ
  rw [projMapData_twistMap]
  exact isIso_twistMap_of_inputs 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 hℓ)
    (tw.injective_twistFibreMap h𝓛 hℓ) (tw.fractionLift h𝓛 hℓ) n

/-- **The domains of definition of the comparisons cover `Proj ℬ`.** This is the scope of the
clause above: as `ℓ` ranges over the degree-one part of the twisting family, the opens `U(ψ_ℓ)`
on which `θ n` is defined and invertible exhaust `Proj ℬ`.

For a twisting module with a global generator a single `ℓ` suffices, which is
`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.mapDomain_twistHom_eq_top`; for a merely invertible one no
single `ℓ` need do, and this is what replaces it. -/
theorem iSup_mapDomain_twistHomOf_eq_top [Module.Invertible R ↥(𝓛 1)] :
    (⨆ x : 𝓛 1, mapDomain 𝒜 ℬ (tw.twistHomOf h𝓛 x.2)) = ⊤ := by
  refine top_le_iff.mp ?_
  rw [← tw.iSup_basicOpen_twistHomOf_eq_top h𝓛]
  refine iSup_le fun p => le_trans ?_ (le_iSup _ p.1)
  exact tw.basicOpen_le_mapDomain_twistHomOf h𝓛 p.1.2 p.2.2.2.1 p.2.2.2.2

end Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist

end
